.TH VIDEODL 1 "September 2026" "videodl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
videodl \- download HTTP media and HLS playlists with a persistent queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B videodl setup
.RI [ --destination " DIR"] " [--config FILE]"
.br
.B videodl add
.RI [ options ] " URL"
.br
.B videodl worker
.RI [ --watch ] " [options]"
.br
.B videodl
.BI --output " FILE"
.RI [ options ] " URL"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads direct HTTP(S) media or public unencrypted HLS playlists.
DASH and advanced media assembly require FFmpeg.
Options must precede positional arguments. Existing output files are never replaced.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Create configuration, local guide, completions, manual and data directories.
Existing configuration is preserved. No daemon is started.
.TP
.B doctor
Read-only configuration, paths and FFmpeg diagnostics; no network access.
.TP
.B add --name NAME URL
Queue a download. Returns a job identifier.
.TP
.B worker [--watch]
Drain queued jobs, or continue watching for new ones.
A failed job does not terminate continuous supervision.
.TP
.B list / status JOB_ID / watch [--once] [--json]
Inspect the queue, a job, or an automatically refreshed report.
.TP
.B retry JOB_ID / cancel JOB_ID
Requeue or cancel a job. Recoverable HTTP partial data is retained.
.TP
.B daemon start|stop|restart|status|logs
Manage the detached background worker.
.TP
.B config init|path|show|get|set|edit
Initialize, locate, inspect or edit settings. Example: config set concurrency 2.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print a shell completion script. See the setup guide for installation.
.TP
.B help [COMMAND] / man
Display help or the embedded plain-text manual.
.SH TRANSFER OPTIONS
.TP
.B --retries N
Extra attempts on transient HTTP/network failures, 0 to 10; default 3.
.TP
.B --resume=false
Disable verified HTTP resume. Default enabled; requires a strong ETag.
.TP
.B --max-height N
HLS resolution ceiling, e.g. 1080. Zero selects the highest bandwidth.
Not supported with DASH or forced --ffmpeg.
.TP
.B --idle-timeout DURATION
Maximum idle read duration, default 60s. FFmpeg uses its network read timeout.
.TP
.B --timeout DURATION
Connection, TLS and HTTP response-header timeout, default 30s.
.TP
.B --concurrency N
Simultaneous queued downloads, 1 through 8; default 1.
.TP
.B --ffmpeg / --ffmpeg-path PATH
Force FFmpeg or select its executable. No byte resume with FFmpeg.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/videodl/config.json
Configuration, overridden by XDG_CONFIG_HOME, VIDEODL_CONFIG or --config.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/videodl/
Queue and logs, overridden by XDG_STATE_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/Downloads/videodl/
Default destination. Configure with config set destination DIR.
.TP
.I DESTINATION/.videodl/
Private HTTP partial files, validators and persistent advisory lock files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Settings accept VIDEODL_ uppercase names, e.g. VIDEODL_RETRIES,
VIDEODL_RESUME, VIDEODL_MAX_HEIGHT and VIDEODL_IDLE_TIMEOUT.
Precedence: defaults, configuration file, environment, command flags.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on invalid configuration, command error or failed one-shot job.
.SH LIMITATIONS
No website extraction or login handling. Native HLS processes a playlist snapshot.
Byte resume is for direct HTTP only; HLS and FFmpeg restart from the beginning.
HTTP partial reuse checks ETag and Content-Range; changed objects restart safely.
